# ArcLite backend
circuits/target/
# The compiled circuit is build output, but the prover needs it at runtime and Noir is not
# available in a Vercel build — so this one artifact is committed and copied into the function
# bundle by the postbuild. Without it the prover throws ENOENT on every settlement, which reads
# as a window that failed rather than a venue that cannot prove at all.
!circuits/artifacts/
ops/node_modules/
contracts/out/
contracts/cache/
contracts/broadcast/
contracts/lib/
.wrangler/
circuits/target/
# The compiled circuit is build output, but the prover needs it at runtime and Noir is not
# available in a Vercel build — so this one artifact is committed and copied into the function
# bundle by the postbuild. Without it the prover throws ENOENT on every settlement, which reads
# as a window that failed rather than a venue that cannot prove at all.
!circuits/artifacts/
circuits/generated/
